## 5. Verification

### [CXC-ICV-ACCEPT] What the Fidelity Pass Must Satisfy

| id | claim | test |
|---|---|---|
| ICV-C1 | pixel-fidelity to the pre-vis | a headless PNG (`python -m composeio.render.engine.runtime intelligence/console/console.compose.yaml --headless /tmp/console.png`) matches the pre-vis INTENT — layout (chat hero + rail), the four voices visually distinct, the semicircle gauge with 4 zones + big readout, the presence avatar, the registered checklist, the ledger grid — reviewed against `console-blended.html` as the golden reference |
| ICV-C2 | bindings still work | every widget's `on_bus_state` + subscribed namespaces + the scene `namespaces:`/bindings are UNCHANGED from the MVP; with `--transports` the thread streams, the gauge tracks `self/context_pct`, the ledger/registered/activity/subagents update live (the fidelity pass touched draw(), never the wiring) |
| ICV-C3 | Canvas-contract-only | no widget imports skia (or any backend); every new draw call is a method on `render/canvas.py`; features with no primitive (letter-spacing, asymmetric radii, dashed borders, the bg grid) use the documented approximations in [CXC-ICV-TOKENS] |
| ICV-C4 | only the gauge warms | at rest, NO rail surface uses ok/warn/crit as decoration; semantic hues appear only as STATE (registered dots, gauge zones, the guidance packet); a golden render at a low context level shows a calm, dim rail with a cool gauge |
| ICV-C5 | the gauge zones + state | at context 90 the gauge shows the crit zone reached, the value dot on the band, the big number crit, the threshold row "65 crossed / 80 crossed / 90 reached·hot", the guidance foot; at 40 the number is ok/cool and no foot shows |
| ICV-C6 | avatar renders every expression, never blank | each `self/avatar/expression` enum value renders a face; an unknown value renders `grounded`; the halo breathes + eyes blink under normal motion |
| ICV-C7 | reduced-motion | with `design.reduced_motion: true`, breathe/blink/beat/hotpulse/runpulse render their REST frame and no clocked widget forces a per-frame redraw |
| ICV-C8 | theme swap | `design.theme: light` renders the fully-specified light tokens with no widget code change; the header button toggles dark↔light and redraws |
| ICV-C9 | new widgets registered + tested | `RegisteredChecklistWidget`, `SelfLedgerWidget`, `AvatarWidget` (+ the semicircle gauge) self-register with the widget registry, parse from the `.compose.yaml`, and each ships a self-test / render test |
| ICV-C10 | the suite stays green | the full existing render test suite passes unchanged; new tests are additive; the mermaid panel degrades to the styled source panel on Skia without breaking the screen ([CXC-ICV-CANVAS] option B) |

