## 6. Build Sequence

### [CXC-ICV-BUILD] The Order Fable Builds In

1. **Design system first** ([CXC-ICV-TOKENS], [CXC-ICV-THEME]) — author `console_theme.py` with both token tables + the `active` selector + the role names. Nothing else is correct until the tokens exist; every later step imports them. Land the reduced-motion + theme plumbing on the RenderContext ([CXC-ICV-MOTION]/[CXC-ICV-THEME]) here.
2. **The hero widgets** — `chat_thread` ([CXC-ICV-CHAT], the four-voice bubbles + harness packets) and the semicircle context gauge ([CXC-ICV-GAUGE]). These are the highest visual leverage and the most-seen; get them right against the golden render before touching the rail.
3. **The rail widgets** — refine `activity` ([CXC-ICV-ACTIVITY]) + `subagent_ledger` ([CXC-ICV-SUBAGENTS]) to the pre-vis rows, then build the NEW `RegisteredChecklistWidget` ([CXC-ICV-REGISTERED]) and `SelfLedgerWidget` ([CXC-ICV-LEDGER]). All four share the header + bordered-panel idiom, so build the shared chrome once.
4. **The avatar + motion** ([CXC-ICV-AVATAR], [CXC-ICV-MOTION]) — the NEW `AvatarWidget` with the expression path sets + the breathe/blink clock ticks, then wire the remaining motion (beat, hotpulse, runpulse) across the header, gauge, and subagents. Verify the reduced-motion gate ([CXC-ICV-ACCEPT] ICV-C7) once all clocked widgets exist.
5. **The scene chrome + mermaid** — the header/brandmark/live-dot/composer + the background grid/wash ([CXC-ICV-CHROME]), then the mermaid/canvas panel ([CXC-ICV-CANVAS]) as option B (styled source panel) with the collapsible chrome; flag option A (the SVG pipeline) to the architect as the fidelity ceiling.
6. **Update the scene** — extend `intelligence/console/console.compose.yaml` to bind the new widgets to their spec-34 §8 namespaces (`self/registered`, the `self/*` ledger set, `self/avatar/expression`, `thread/diagram`) and set `theme`/`reduced_motion`. Bindings are ADDED, never rewritten.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CONSOLE-VISUAL]

