**Status**: DRAFT for review (2026-07-19). The complete build brief for the VISUAL-FIDELITY pass of the
Intelligence Console WORK flavor: take the functional MVP (real bus bindings, stock widget chrome) and make it
match the approved blended pre-vis ([CXC-ICD-D17]) WITHOUT touching the proven wiring ([CXC-ICV-INTENT]). One
design-system module of record — every hex (both themes), typography role, spacing step, radius, elevation, and
motion timing lifted verbatim from `console-blended.html` ([CXC-ICV-TOKENS]) — then one fidelity node per surface:
the four-voice chat hero + harness packets ([CXC-ICV-CHAT]), the semicircle context gauge (the one surface allowed
to warm, [CXC-ICV-GAUGE]), the NEW registered checklist ([CXC-ICV-REGISTERED]) + self/ledger grid ([CXC-ICV-LEDGER]),
refined activity/subagents rows ([CXC-ICV-ACTIVITY]/[CXC-ICV-SUBAGENTS]), the NEW self-animated avatar with shared
expression enum + breathe/blink ([CXC-ICV-AVATAR]), the mermaid/canvas panel with its degrade risk flagged
([CXC-ICV-CANVAS]), and the scene shell ([CXC-ICV-CHROME]). Motion is scene-graph animation with a new
reduced-motion gate ([CXC-ICV-MOTION]); theme is a token swap, not a cascade ([CXC-ICV-THEME]). Acceptance is
pixel-fidelity-to-intent + bindings-still-work + Canvas-contract-only + suite-green ([CXC-ICV-ACCEPT]); the build
order runs tokens → hero → rail → avatar/motion → chrome/mermaid → scene ([CXC-ICV-BUILD]).

**Architect — ratifications flagged:** (1) new node-prefix `CXC-ICV-` (Intelligence Console Visual), a `CXC-`
sub-family sibling to `CXC-IC-`/`CXC-ICD-` — needs a [CONV-PREFIX] row before lint. (2) the mermaid-on-Skia
call ([CXC-ICV-CANVAS]): ship option B (styled source-degrade) now, or block the fidelity pass on option A (the
headless mermaid→SVG→SvgWidget pipeline, a Node dependency) — recommend B now, A as the later ceiling.
(3) whether the semicircle gauge is a new `context_gauge` widget or a `style:` mode on the existing `gauge`
(recommend a new subclass so the 270° dial stays available). (4) the reduced-motion flag as a `design.reduced_motion`
scene key + RenderContext plumbing is NEW engine surface (no `reduced_motion` exists today) — confirm the key name.
